A||||3||Adrift||Coding your own door locks?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-30-2001||02:25 AM||||I just bought a pair of replacement door locks (NAPA wanted $45 a lock, GM Dealer wanted $40 a lock, Canadian tire wanted $15 a lock!) and need to get them coded. Can I do this myself? Anyone have instructions? Or should I just bring it to a locksmith?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-30-2001||02:33 AM||||Just take 'em to a lock smith.  They do this stuff for a living so there's not much chance of a screw up.  (Ever changed the door locks?  You don't want to do it a second time because you coded them wrong.)  The FS sells the door locks for less than 20 bucks USD.  If the GM dealership charged you 40 bucks, they pulled your pants down.  Lots cheaper at my local dealership.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||11-30-2001||06:11 AM||||the dealer I usually get my locks from does them for me for free mostly. once in a while if its a diff guy, i get charged $25 for the set.<BR> on a side note, lots of the newer cars can only get locks as a set (ie doors, ign, trunk, etc) I needed one for an Explorer and they said $200+ for the whole set, couldnt get just one.......so off I went to the junkyard.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||11-30-2001||10:08 AM||||I got my doorlocks for $15 CAN each, which is about $9 US||||reg||1
